3 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82541c-40ca-5df9-aa17-c20b201fadd4" :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at a General Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24554dd2-c7a7-5795-ace8-ef8ee8123e65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos(\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287345} {:answer/id #uuid "5a761898-639e-58fc-b2fd-c7718ff280db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\cos(\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24554dd2-c7a7-5795-ace8-ef8ee8123e65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos(\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287345} :answer-field/id #uuid "2071a2f6-650b-5c57-86b4-17df74f93151" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66173e3f-74f3-53c0-ad15-c0b28d4d1d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sin(\\theta)+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66173e3f-74f3-53c0-ad15-c0b28d4d1d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sin(\\theta)+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287348} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6c69d3-7405-5114-a936-18767e95e99d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca5b2e3e-ddb1-5792-98f6-dd4e9edd115c" :question/math-academy-id "q-327171" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/61ffc8879681a1d0bb381f32178ea2e7b58e251341b2280ba607448231458dc5.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(0,5)$ with horizontal radius $3$ and vertical radius $8,$ as shown above. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ that traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(3,5).$\n\n$x=$ \n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$ \n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(0,5),$ $a=3$ and $b=8.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db20f4a5-27a4-5fbc-aae2-2febf8f99cb1" :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "582cfdb3-9e7d-5f15-a26a-d00ec9f67751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287370} {:answer/id #uuid "cd12cacf-3474-5a8a-8a58-48b6696f9204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287371} {:answer/id #uuid "69ea148e-dfc2-5dd4-bbfe-d1130acc22ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287372} {:answer/id #uuid "3a98dff9-85fe-5c45-bae9-9e80401d71b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287373} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a87621-cfad-513c-8bc6-4e1fddf2fcfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9a87621-cfad-513c-8bc6-4e1fddf2fcfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287374} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec9984a4-cf5d-59d7-aabc-48c476f6a41a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99d45658-64c1-527b-ba91-3ee0b91560a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-6880" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/86dcfa13b7863c08b348855e776a6df709ecac499af02c2479cfdf484eeaf328.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate the ellipse shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=4$ and $b=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db20f4a5-27a4-5fbc-aae2-2febf8f99cb1" :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95eae759-7706-57f4-88d2-511815ad1f0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287384} {:answer/id #uuid "3826e7f2-0ee1-5ea7-be8b-75e912241519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287385} {:answer/id #uuid "f263f1c5-c023-52c5-b17c-3b36f00f05e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287386} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4f07ea-3198-56ba-ae69-7e96fd25c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287387} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab376a3-3e60-5149-ae06-fc3d45c3c97f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c4f07ea-3198-56ba-ae69-7e96fd25c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287387} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e87eca0-e8ca-545a-beab-0c3a297aa01b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9798ed5-9467-5b84-a966-140686dec581" :question/math-academy-id "q-79281" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/ac2bba143473bc68e3a578c008a5de3cc36727d984bfba5d5e0da95462c08f77.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal radius $2$ and vertical radius $4,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(2,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, $a=2$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}]}
